vtpm-mds (0.3.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * devid-enroll: a renewal by the packaged oneshot (root) keeps the owner
    and group of each DevID file it replaces, or gives a new file those of
    the output directory, so a SPIRE agent running as its own user can still
    read them. Files that 0.3.0 already left owned by root keep that owner:
    chown them to the agent's user once, or move them aside.
  * devid-enroll: the SPIRE agent restart after a new LDevID is queued
    (systemctl --no-block try-restart) instead of awaited; the oneshot,
    ordered before spire-agent, no longer waits on it until its start
    timeout.
  * devid-enroll: -tpm defaults to /dev/tpmrm0, so the kernel resource
    manager flushes what a killed run left loaded in the TPM.
  * vtpm-mds: no change.

 -- Andreas Dembach <andreas.dembach@dg-i.net>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 20:49:44 +0200

vtpm-mds (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BREAKING: the daemon runs as the system user vtpm-mds (extra group
    www-data) with only CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE in a hardened unit: the file
    system is read-only except /var/lib/vtpm-mds, and traffic is limited to
    169.254.0.0/16 and localhost, so listen_addr must be link-local. The
    DevID CA key is read by systemd from
    /etc/ssl/private/proxmox_devid_ca.key and handed over as the credential
    devid_ca.key; a missing file stops the start (243/CREDENTIALS). A key
    elsewhere needs a drop-in that first resets LoadCredential=.
  * BREAKING: config.yaml and the YAML inventory are decoded strictly; an
    unknown config key stops the start.
  * BREAKING: callers bound to no VM are refused (mds.require_vm_identity,
    default true). /latest/attest, /latest/identity, /.well-known/jwks.json
    and instance-identity/signature are removed.
  * DevID: the EK certificate is bound to the endorsement key; the LDevID
    subject is CN=<VM ID> only; the EK is pinned per VM on first enrolment
    ($STATE_DIRECTORY/ek-pins; delete the VM's pin after replacing its
    vTPM); LDevIDs expire after mds.devid_lifetime (default 2160h) and
    guests renew them with devid-enroll.timer; the DevID CA must be a CA
    whose key matches (one intermediate per cluster); the issued PEM
    carries leaf + intermediate.
  * devid-enroll derives the DevID parent from SPIRE's SRK template and no
    longer touches or evicts persistent handles.
  * devid-enroll now ships devid-enroll.service (before spire-agent, on
    every boot) and a daily devid-enroll.timer, enabled on install. On a new
    LDevID they clear SPIRE's agent SVID cache and try-restart spire-agent.
    Output and SPIRE data directories are set in /etc/default/devid-enroll.
  * New binary and unit vtpm-mds-bind: binds each guest NIC on vmbr_imds to
    its configured MAC in the nftables table "bridge vtpm_mds_bind".
  * Metadata: VM tags under tags/instance/, node topology under placement/,
    public-ipv4 only when declared; guest configs read from this node only
    and reloaded within 5 s of a change.
  * Operations: per-peer throttling (429), one access line per request and
    one line per issued LDevID, debug lines only with -debug, honest
    /health status, a clean exit on stop, and a running daemon restarted
    after an upgrade.

 -- Andreas Dembach <andreas.dembach@dg-i.net>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:06:38 +0200

vtpm-mds (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Split the source into two binary packages: vtpm-mds (hypervisor daemon,
    legacy aliases prox-mds and qemu-mds, systemd unit, /etc/vtpm-mds
    config and /var/lib/vtpm-mds state) and devid-enroll (guest DevID
    enrollment client and its man page only).
  * BREAKING: upgrading vtpm-mds no longer leaves /usr/bin/devid-enroll on
    the host. Guests install devid-enroll_*.deb instead; hypervisors keep
    installing vtpm-mds_*.deb only.
  * devid-enroll declares Breaks/Replaces: vtpm-mds (<< 0.2.0) so the move
    of /usr/bin/devid-enroll off the host package unpacks cleanly. Neither
    package depends on or recommends the other.
  * devid-enroll installs no systemd unit and no IMDS listener, so it is
    safe to install inside guest images.

 -- Andreas Dembach <andreas.dembach@dg-i.net>  Sun, 20 Sep 2026 12:15:57 +0200

vtpm-mds (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian packaging. debian/ was referenced by `make deb` /
    dpkg-buildpackage but never committed; this restores a native package
    with a systemd unit and Proxmox-oriented install layout.
  * Install /usr/sbin/vtpm-mds (aliases prox-mds, qemu-mds),
    /usr/bin/devid-enroll, /etc/vtpm-mds/config.yaml (listen
    169.254.169.1:80, Proxmox /etc/pve inventory, host swTPM PKI paths),
    and /lib/systemd/system/vtpm-mds.service.

